test_poisson_lagrit -- del_vor against LaGriT on Poisson disk meshes (Nov 2026)
=======================================================================

QUICK START

  sh run_poisson_lagrit_tests.sh [path-to-del_vor]    10 runs, about 2 s
  open summary.html

WHAT IS TESTED

  Five meshes from LaGriT's suites (inputs/, from Carl Gable; see
  inputs/NOTICE). Cases 1 and 2 of test/suite/test_poisson_3d, box
  reduced to 0.4 x 0.4 x 0.2:

    test_3d_poi_01   1647 vertices, 7788 tets; no buffer on the
                     outside surfaces: 75 negative coefficients
    test_3d_poi_02   1870 vertices, 9056 tets; buffer = h: the
                     boundary vertices lie on a grid, 871 zero-area
                     connections, no negative coefficients

  and the three meshes of test/suite/test_poisson_2d, unit square:

    output01_square_uniform   257 vertices, 432 triangles, h = 0.05
    output02_square_var       2109 vertices, 4071 triangles, variable
                              h (h0 = 0.01, WIDTH_FACTOR 10)
    output03_square_var       1088 vertices, 2087 triangles,
                              WIDTH_FACTOR 20

  del_vor -avs MESH.inp -stor MESH_keep.stor -zero_area keep
          -compress off
  del_vor -avs MESH.inp -stor MESH.stor          (the defaults)

  against the .stor files LaGriT wrote (dump / stor: anothermatbld3d
  in 3D, matbld2d in 2D).

WHAT IS CHECKED (check_poisson_lagrit.py)

  The checks allow exactly what LaGriT's writer explains:

  3D  anothermatbld3d merges coefficients within 1e-8 of the largest
      |A/d| when it compresses, and leaves out coefficients below 1e-8
      of the largest: coefficients to 1.01e-8.
  2D  matbld2d writes every value, but LaGriT computed from the full
      coordinates and the .inp files keep 13 digits. Rounding the
      coordinates again at the 13th digit moves del_vor's own
      results by up to 3e-11: coefficients to 5e-11.

  box_volume     del_vor's volumes add up to the exact volume (0.032)
                 or area (1), to 1e-13
  pairs          every LaGriT pair is in del_vor's file; every pair
                 LaGriT left out has |A/d| <= 1e-8 max (3D), none (2D)
  coef_diff      common pairs within the tolerance above
  vol_diff       volumes within 1e-11 of the largest, except at the
                 vertices of nonzero pairs LaGriT left out (MEASURED)
  negative       the same negative pairs in both files
  default_zero   del_vor's default leaves out exactly its zero-area
                 pairs, all of which LaGriT left out too

WHAT WAS FOUND (Nov 8 2026)

  - Most pairs agree to 1e-13; only those LaGriT's compression merged
    differ, by up to 9.9e-9 of the largest (histograms).
  - Case 1: LaGriT left out two real, tiny connections (1500-1591 and
    1186-1266, A/d about 1e-10 and 5e-10 of the largest) and their
    shares of the four vertices' volumes, so LaGriT's volumes add up
    to 0.032 + 5.8e-13. del_vor keeps both; its volumes add up to
    0.032 exactly (2e-15).
  - Case 2: both codes leave out the same 871 zero-area connections.
  - 2D: the same connections, no negative or zero-area ones;
    coefficients agree to 8.4e-12, volumes to 9.3e-13, most pairs to
    1e-13. The largest differences are in the smallest triangles (the
    coordinate rounding matters most there).

